2026-09-06T00:00Z claude created

--- body ---
## Context

Fable 5.1 deep-QA pass (2026-09-06). The duration sample timer starts
before `ensure()`, which itself MD5-hashes the file, reads/validates any
existing pack, and enqueues behind other native work (not priority). A
native job slipping in during that window (e.g. hashing a large file
elsewhere) is booked entirely as this document's extraction time. With
only 3 samples the 95th percentile is the max observed rate, so one such
inflated sample dominates the upper bound and, because the cache keeps
only the latest observation per attachment and the attachment is now
`current`, it is never re-measured -- the poisoned estimate persists
across sessions until a processor version bump invalidates it.

## Work

- Start timing from the first real progress signal (`onProgress`'s first
  tick) rather than from before `ensure()` is even called, or otherwise
  exclude pre-enqueue time from the recorded sample.
- Consider discarding a sample if `workerBusy()` was true at any point
  before the document's first progress tick, since queue contention time
  is not a property of the document.

## Acceptance

- [ ] A synthetic slow pre-enqueue phase (hash + queue wait) followed by
      a fast real extraction produces a sample close to the real
      extraction time, not the combined time, in a test with an
      injectable clock.
- [ ] Existing duration-estimation tests still pass.
